  "findings": [
    "Exact 55% agreement is too low to treat the per-cell Pass B matrix as a precise measurement instrument.",
    "The independent coder is not uniformly more skeptical: it often maps historical analogies to SUPPORTS more aggressively, especially S7. This is evidence that several invariant definitions are semantically elastic rather than evidence that primary coding was simply too positive.",
    "S1 and S10 have comparatively stable exact coding; S6 and S3 are much less stable. S6's 1/12 exact agreement makes any HD1 frequency claim for that invariant unreliable.",
    "SUPPORTS versus NARROWS is especially unstable, so HD1 should preserve the qualitative narrowing arguments but not use raw support counts as a convergence score.",
    "Both coders produce zero direct CONTRADICTS on the 12 Deep Anchors. This does not prove universality; it increases concern that the frozen hypotheses are high-level guardrails with weak falsifiability at single-case retrospective resolution.",
    "Negative controls matter: primary coding leaves S5 largely N/A and F4 has zero HD1 historical anti-law evidence. Cross-era work must continue to preserve domain-limited hypotheses rather than maximizing apparent recurrence."
  ],
  "disposition": {
    "doNot": "Do not aggregate HD1 support counts into a universal historical convergence score or update S1-S10 definitions mid-campaign.",
    "retain": "Retain primary Pass B as one explicit interpretation, retain independent coding as a disagreement witness, and treat the disagreement itself as evidence about measurement/codebook uncertainty.",
    "strongerEvidenceOrder": [
      "source-native historical facts and rival/failure evidence",
      "prospective replay prediction errors",
      "recurrent residual structures across later epochs",
      "stable cross-coder applicability relations",
      "exact SUPPORTS/NARROWS counts"
    ]
  },
  "worldModelUpdate": "Historical OOD dogfood currently supports the existence of recurring structural pressures more strongly than it supports a precise fixed taxonomy. A stable reality structure can exist while our labels remain unstable; convergence of Reality must not be inferred from convergence of our classifier."
